# VALIDATION LOG — Person 1 Class-Imbalance Experiments
# Protocol: Execute -> Validate -> Debug/Rerun -> Validate -> Continue
# Random seed: 42 everywhere. Frozen test set: n=499,641 (No=414,633 / Yes=85,008).

## STEP 1 — Data inspection (PASS)
- File: brfss_master.parquet (8,647,149 bytes, downloaded from connected Google Drive; id matched user-supplied share link).
- Rows: 2,498,203 | Columns: 17
- Columns: YEAR, DIABETE4, EXERANY2, _MICHD, ASTHMA3, ADDEPEV3, CHCKDNY2, MARITAL,
  _EDUCAG, DRNKANY6, _AGEG5YR, _BMI5CAT, _INCOMG1, _RFSMOK3, GENHLTH, HAVARTH4, SEXVAR
- Target DIABETE4 binary: No = 2,073,163 (83.0%), Yes = 425,040 (17.0%).
  Counts sum to 2,498,203 exactly (validated: 2073163+425040=2498203). Imbalance ratio 4.878:1.
- Missing values: 0 in all columns. Constant/near-constant columns: none.
- Duplicate rows: 1,045,135 exact analytical-profile duplicates. Per documented prior audit
  (person1_final_handoff_status.csv, Drive): duplicate analytical profiles are NOT treated as
  duplicate respondents; STATE+SEQNO audit found 0 duplicate respondent groups. Master has no
  STATE/SEQNO columns, so respondent-level dedup cannot be re-verified here; analytical
  duplicates retained per documented methodology. No accidental duplicates introduced by us.
- Year coverage: 2014..2024 all 11 years present (2014:201,035 ... 2024:224,730).
  DEVIATION vs nominal title "2015-2024": actual master covers 2014-2024; all years 2015-2024
  ARE represented. Using the master as-is; deviation documented in final report.
- No suspicious values (all codes within documented BRFSS ranges; no negatives).

## STEP 2 — Preprocessing (protocol defined; PASS)
- CORRECTION 1 (7/9 filter): downloaded prior preprocessing.py contained
  `df[RESEARCH_VARIABLES].isin([7,9])` row removal. In the MASTER parquet, codes 7 and 9
  appear only in _AGEG5YR (222,573 and 297,254 rows) where they are VALID age categories
  (50-54, 60-64). Applying the raw-XPT filter to the already-standardized master would
  wrongly discard ~20% of valid rows. Decision: do NOT apply the 7/9 filter to the master.
  The master is already standardized (matches prior handoff PASS audit: 2,498,203 rows,
  17 cols, 0 missing, DIABETE4 No/Yes, 2014-2024, zero respondent duplicates).
- Applied: age restriction _AGEG5YR>=5 (kept 2,498,203/2,498,203; min already 5.0),
  complete-case dropna (no-op, 0 missing).
- DEVIATION — Group 1 artifacts: Drive searched for 'BRFSS', 'Group 1/Group_1/group1',
  'Person_1/Person1', 'preprocessing'. No Group 1 preprocessing code, notebook, or results
  found in Drive or ~/workspace. Only prior-session Person-1 artifacts
  (preprocessing.py, preprocessing_summary.csv, person1_final_handoff_status.csv,
  PERSON_1_HANDOFF folders) were found and were used as methodology reference.
  Therefore Group 1's exact preprocessing/models/seeds CANNOT be reproduced; a clean,
  defensible protocol is defined and documented here instead (no claim of reproducing Group 1).
- Target: DIABETE4 -> y = 1 if "Yes" else 0.
- Features: 15 research variables (EXERANY2, _MICHD, ASTHMA3, ADDEPEV3, CHCKDNY2, MARITAL,
  _EDUCAG, DRNKANY6, _AGEG5YR, _BMI5CAT, _INCOMG1, _RFSMOK3, GENHLTH, HAVARTH4, SEXVAR).
  YEAR excluded as metadata (not a patient-level predictor; consistent with the documented
  RESEARCH_VARIABLES list which excludes YEAR).
- Feature encoding: integer-coded categoricals kept as int; no one-hot.
- Split: stratified 80/20, shuffle=True, random_state=42 BEFORE any resampling.
  Train = 1,998,562 (No 1,658,530 / Yes 340,032); Test = 499,641 (No 414,633 / Yes 85,008).
- Split validations: sizes sum to 2,498,203; zero index overlap; target not in predictors;
  identical frozen feature column order for train/test; same class proportions in train and test.
- Models (documented hyperparameters, random_state=42):
  LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000) + StandardScaler (scaler fit on TRAIN only);
  RandomForest(n_estimators=100, max_depth=12, n_jobs=-1);
  XGBClassifier(n_estimators=300, max_depth=6, lr=0.05, subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.8,
  tree_method='hist', eval_metric='logloss', n_jobs=-1).
- Scale decision: full 2.5M-row training used (no downsampling). Benchmarks on 200k:
  LR 0.2s, RF 9.1s, XGB 6.1s -> full-data fits feasible.
- No target leakage: all predictors are BRFSS health/demographic variables; target column
  never present in feature matrices (asserted in code).

