## STEP 5 - SMOTE (PASS)
- CORRECTION: SMOTENC attempted first (categorical-aware was the plan) but
  imbalanced-learn 0.14.2 raised ValueError: "SMOTE-NC is not designed to work only
  with categorical features. It requires some numerical features." All 15 BRFSS
  features are integer-coded categoricals. -> Standard SMOTE(k_neighbors=5) used on
  integer codes (published BRFSS-SMOTE convention); config + docstrings updated.
- Applied to TRAIN ONLY after the split. Before: No=1,658,530 / Yes=340,032.
  After: 1,658,530 / 1,658,530 (exact parity); +1,318,498 synthetic samples;
  final train 3,317,060. Synthetic values validated within observed per-feature
  [min,max]; no NaN/inf; 15 features unchanged.
- Metrics (test): LR acc=0.7001 prec=0.3231 rec=0.6965 f1=0.4414 roc=0.7698 prauc=0.3991;
  RF acc=0.6854 prec=0.3168 rec=0.7342 f1=0.4426 roc=0.7762 prauc=0.4108;
  XGB acc=0.6841 prec=0.3156 rec=0.7334 f1=0.4413 roc=0.7756 prauc=0.4104.
- Results saved to 05_SMOTE/results_smote.csv.

